# Configures one-way TLS (server authentication) for the gRPC subsystem.
#
# Uses the WildFly security command to create the necessary Elytron resources:
#   - key-store: loads server.keystore.p12 from the server configuration directory
#   - key-manager: wraps the key-store to provide the server's TLS identity
#   - server-ssl-context: TLS context using the key-manager; client auth is not required
#   - https-listener: binds the SSL context to the HTTPS socket with HTTP/2 enabled
#
# Run configure-elytron-mutual-tls.cli afterward to enable mutual TLS (mTLS).

# Guard on the https-listener: if it already exists, skip the whole setup
if (outcome != success) of /subsystem=undertow/server=default-server/https-listener=https:read-resource
    security enable-ssl-http-server --key-store-path=server.keystore.p12 --key-store-path-relative-to=jboss.server.config.dir --key-store-password=secret --new-key-store-name=grpc-key-store --new-key-manager-name=grpc-key-manager --new-ssl-context-name=grpc-ssl-context --add-https-listener --no-reload
    /subsystem=undertow/server=default-server/https-listener=https:write-attribute(name=enable-http2, value=true)
end-if
